> Anyone know what the difference between M1_SWIM and M1_AMPHIBIOUS are 
> from the file src/mondata.h?  Their descriptions are the following ...
> 
> 
> #define M1_SWIM         0x00000002L     /* can traverse water */
> #define M1_AMPHIBIOUS   0x00000200L     /* can survive underwater */
> 
> Is there a creature that is amphibious but cannot swim?  I.e. some sort of 
> unbreathing creature that doesn't like water and can't move in it but can 
> survive because it doesn't need to breathe?  Anyone got any specific 
> examples of this?  Thanks!

Swimmers must stay in the water (like fish, eels, etc.) or they start
losing HPs (like giant/electric eels on land).  Amphibians can just as
easily live on land or in the water (most snakes).  Think RL
amphibians vs. fish.  So no, there are no amphibians that cannot swim,
but plenty of swimmers that aren't amphibious!

